menu "mi_mqtt"

config MI_MQTT_HAVE_ESP_BROKER_LIVENESS
    bool "esp-mqtt provides broker-liveness / pingresp-diag extension API"
    default n
    help
      Enable only when the project's esp-mqtt ("mqtt") component is the
      patched fork that exposes the broker-liveness / pingresp-diagnostics
      extension API:
        - esp_mqtt_client_get_broker_liveness()
        - esp_mqtt_client_get_pingresp_state()
        - esp_mqtt_client_get_pingresp_diag()
        - esp_mqtt_broker_liveness_t / esp_mqtt_broker_liveness_snapshot_t

      Stock ESP-IDF esp-mqtt does NOT provide these symbols. Leave this
      disabled (default) to compile mi_mqtt against stock esp-mqtt: the
      broker-liveness / pingresp snapshots then degrade gracefully —
      Mqtt_Client_Broker_Liveness_Snapshot() reports the broker as READY
      whenever the MQTT app layer is connected, deferring connection health
      to esp-mqtt's built-in keepalive. The enhanced dead-broker detection /
      force-reconnect watchdog is simply inactive in that mode.

endmenu
